{{!-- First-party page written for Volta (Qompass AI, 2026). --}}
{{#> layout }}
  <h2>{{ text "API" }}</h2>

  <p>Volta speaks the two protocols OpenPGP clients already use:</p>

  <h3>Verifying Keyserver (VKS) API</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><code>GET /vks/v1/by-fingerprint/&lt;fingerprint&gt;</code></li>
    <li><code>GET /vks/v1/by-keyid/&lt;key-id&gt;</code></li>
    <li><code>GET /vks/v1/by-email/&lt;address&gt;</code></li>
    <li><code>POST /vks/v1/upload</code> — upload a key (JSON body with a
      <code>keytext</code> field)</li>
    <li><code>POST /vks/v1/request-verify</code> — request verification
      emails for the uploaded key's addresses</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>HKP</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><code>GET /pks/lookup?op=get&amp;search=&lt;query&gt;</code></li>
    <li><code>GET /pks/lookup?op=index&amp;search=&lt;query&gt;</code></li>
    <li><code>POST /pks/add</code> — submit an armored key</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Web Key Directory (WKD)</h3>
  <p>
    Keys with a verified address are also available through the Web Key
    Directory under
    <code>/.well-known/openpgpkey/&lt;domain&gt;/hu/&lt;hash&gt;</code>,
    with the policy file at
    <code>/.well-known/openpgpkey/&lt;domain&gt;/policy</code>.
  </p>
{{/layout}}
